Unix utility 'deluser'

The Unix utility 'deluser' removes a user account from the user database. Only an
administrative (root) user can run it, and it always asks for confirmation (y/n) before
actually removing the account. The root account itself can never be removed this way.

USAGE:

deluser <user>

For more information, enter 'deluser ?' or 'deluser --help'.

HISTORY

This command appeared in the Hexagonix Dormin development branch (2026).

